<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prithviraj Raso</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prithviraj Raso is an epic poem in Brajbhasha attributed to Chand Bardai, said to have been the court poet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a>. It tells, with much legend, of Prithviraj's life, his elopement with Samyukta and his wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a>. The surviving versions date from the 16th century or later, but the work has deeply shaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> historical memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prithviraj-raso.jpg" alt="Prithviraj Raso" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: अजीत कुमार तिवारी · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prithviraj_Raso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
